<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34335" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπηδ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>jump upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτῇ ἐχούσῃ ἐν γαστρί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.32
				</span></i>
			: metaph. of sense-impressions, <i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				8.2.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. εἰς</span> . . <i>leap</i> or
				<i>spring into</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὴν ναῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermipp.
					54
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.8.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> abs.,
				<i>beat</i>, of the heart, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.67
			</span></i>: aor.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπηδήσας</span>
			<i>eagerly, greedily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				20
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
